% optim: the sat module's objective options $max/$min, on the
% smallest instance that can tell. Demonstrates that the compiled
% branch-and-bound engine inside the built-in library is active for
% solve([$max(P)], [Vars]) (and symmetrically $min), and works
% unchanged through external solvers and portfolios.
%
% Problem: 2 items, capacity 2.
%   item 1: weight 1, value 3
%   item 2: weight 2, value 5
% Every feasible pack: value 0 (neither), 3 (item 1), 5 (item 2).
% The optimum is 5 (take item 2; weight 2 <= 2).
%
% Verified result on the current binary: P = 5 on the built-in
% solver, kissat and cadical. With SATDBG=1 the run shows three
% engine solves (first model, lifted bound, retrieval of the best
% model) instead of one -- this is the optimization loop working,
% and the objective value no longer depends on which model the
% engine happens to find first.
%
% Gotcha: the objective option belongs to the OPTIONS list of
% solve/2. Passing it as a member of the VARIABLES list of solve/1,
% e.g. solve([$max(P), [X1, X2, P]]), is a plain SAT solve (the
% objective is simply ignored) -- that is how $max first appeared
% to do nothing, until the call was written as solve([$max(P)], ...).
%
% Run:
%   picat exs/satext/optim.pi
%   SATEXT_SOLVER=kissat picat exs/satext/optim.pi
%   SATEXT_SOLVER=cadical picat exs/satext/optim.pi
%   SATDBG=1 picat exs/satext/optim.pi            (show the 3 solves)
%   SATEXT_SOLVER="kissat|cadical" SATEXT_PRT_MIN=1 SATEXT_PRT_STATS=1 \
%       picat exs/satext/optim.pi                 (portfolio races each)

import sat.

main =>
    X1 :: 0..1,
    X2 :: 0..1,
    1 * X1 + 2 * X2 #<= 2,        % weight budget (capacity 2)
    P #= 3 * X1 + 5 * X2,         % objective as a constraint
    writef("objective: $max(P)  --  true optimum of this instance is 5%n"),
    solve([$max(P)], [X1, X2, P]),
    writef("result: X1=%d X2=%d P=%d%n", X1, X2, P),
    ((P == 5) -> writef("OK: optimum 5 found%n")
    ;
     writef("UNEXPECTED: $max reported P=%d, but the optimum is 5%n", P),
     writef("(check the call form: it must be solve([$max(P)], [Vars]))%n"),
     halt).
